Core concepts
    Public client (no secret stored in browser) + PKCE handshake replaces client secret
    Authorization Code Flow: Browser redirects to Keycloak → user logs in → browser gets code → SPA exchanges code for tokens
    Tokens in memory (not cookies) → access/refresh tokens stored in JS variables, not localStorage (XSS risk)
    Configuration: Use pkceMethod: "S256" in keycloak-js init options  medium
    No BFF needed: The official keycloak-js library + Angular adapter handle this directly
Libraries
    keycloak-js + keycloak-angular for Angular
    Or raw keycloak-js for vanilla JS/TS
Edge case: Silent SSO (check-sso) breaks on modern browsers blocking third-party cookies—disable checkLoginIframe or use onLoad: 'login-required' if needed

