Single-page applications face a fundamental security problem: they run entirely
in the browser, an environment where secrets cannot be kept. Storing OAuth
tokens in localStorage or sessionStorage exposes them to cross-site scripting
(XSS) attacks. The Backend-for-Frontend (BFF) pattern solves this by
introducing a thin server-side layer that handles authentication on behalf of
the frontend, keeping tokens where they belong — on the server.
